# Code-Correction-System
This is a code correction system that uses a pre-trained model to correct the syntax and logic errors in the given code. The system takes the buggy code as input and outputs the corrected code as output. The system is designed to be used by developers who are new to programming or who are struggling with syntax and logic errors in their code.

The system is built using Python and the Hugging Face Transformers library. The pre-trained model used by the system is a BERT model that has been fine-tuned on a dataset of code correction tasks. The model is trained to predict the correct syntax and logic for a given code snippet.

To use the system, the user needs to provide the buggy code as input. The system then uses the pre-trained model to correct the syntax and logic errors in the code. The corrected code is then outputted as the final result.

The system is designed to be user-friendly and easy to use. The user interface is simple and intuitive, and the system provides clear and concise feedback on the corrected code. The system also provides a detailed explanation of the errors in the original code and the corrections made by the system.

The system is designed to be scalable and can handle large amounts of code. The system can be used to correct code in a variety of programming languages, including Python, Java, C++, and JavaScript.

The system is also designed to be extensible. The user can add new code correction tasks to the dataset used to train the model, and the model can be fine-tuned to handle these new tasks. This allows the system to be customized to the specific needs of the user.

Overall, the Code Correction System is a powerful tool for developers who are struggling with syntax and logic errors in their code. The system is easy to use, scalable, and extensible, and it provides clear and concise feedback on the corrected code. The system is designed to help developers improve their coding skills and produce high-quality code.
