# Code Correction Challenge

This repository contains a collection of coding problems where you are tasked with correcting buggy code snippets. Each problem is accompanied by a detailed instruction and a test case to validate your solution.

## How to Contribute

1. **Fork the Repository**: Click the "Fork" button at the top right of this repository to create your own copy.

2. **Clone Your Fork**: Clone your forked repository to your local machine using the following command:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/code-correction-challenge.git
   ```

3. **Create a New Branch**: Create a new branch for your solution using the following command:
   ```
   git checkout -b solution-<problem-number>
   ```

4. **Solve the Problem**: Write your solution in the provided code snippet. Ensure that your solution adheres to the specified programming language syntax and logic requirements.

5. **Test Your Solution**: Validate your solution against the provided test case to ensure its accuracy.

6. **Commit Your Changes**: Commit your changes with a descriptive commit message using the following command:
   ```
   git commit -m "Solved problem <problem-number>"
   ```

7. **Push Your Changes**: Push your changes to your forked repository using the following command:
   ```
   git push origin solution-<problem-number>
   ```

8. **Create a Pull Request**: Go to your forked repository on GitHub and click the "New Pull Request" button. Follow the prompts to create a pull request to merge your solution into the main repository.

9. **Wait for Review**: Your pull request will be reviewed by the maintainers. Once approved, your solution will be merged into the main repository.

