# Code Correction Challenge

This repository contains a collection of coding problems designed to test your ability to identify and correct errors in code. Each problem is accompanied by a description of the issue and a set of test cases to validate your solution.

## How to Use

1. **Clone the Repository**: Clone this repository to your local machine using the following command:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/code-correction-challenge.git
   ```

2. **Navigate to the Problem Directory**: Each problem is contained in a separate directory. Navigate to the directory of the problem you want to solve.

3. **Read the Problem Description**: Read the problem description and understand the issue that needs to be corrected.

4. **Write Your Solution**: Write your solution in the provided code file. Ensure that your solution adheres to the specified programming language syntax and logic requirements.

5. **Validate Your Solution**: Run your solution against the provided test cases to ensure its accuracy. You can use the test cases provided in the problem description or create your own test cases.

6. **Submit Your Solution**: Once you have a working solution, submit it by creating a pull request to this repository.

