# Code Snippet Correction

This repository contains a collection of code snippets that have been identified as having errors or bugs. The goal of this project is to provide a platform for developers to practice their coding skills by identifying and correcting these errors.

## How to Contribute

1. Fork this repository to your own GitHub account.
2. Clone the forked repository to your local machine.
3. Create a new branch for your correction.
4. Identify a code snippet that you would like to correct.
5. Make the necessary changes to the code snippet to fix the error.
6. Test your correction to ensure that it works as expected.
7. Commit your changes with a descriptive commit message.
8. Push your changes to your forked repository.
9. Create a pull request to merge your changes into the main repository.

## Guidelines for Correction

- Your correction should be based on the original code snippet provided.
- Ensure that your correction adheres to the original programming language syntax and logic requirements.
- Validate your solution against the provided test cases to ensure its accuracy.
- Your solution should strictly consist of the corrected code only.
- Wrap your code using ``` to maintain proper formatting.

## Example

Below is an example of a code snippet that has been identified as having an error:

```java
public class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");
    }
}
```

The above code snippet is correct and does not require any correction.

## Test Cases

To ensure the accuracy of your correction, you should validate your solution against the provided test cases. Below is an example of a test case:

Input: 5 1
1
2
3
4
5

Output: 1 3 6 10 15

## Contributing

Contributions are welcome! If you find any errors or bugs in the code snippets, please feel free to create an issue or submit a pull request. We appreciate your help in improving this project.

## License

This project is licensed under the MIT License. See the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details.

## Acknowledgments

- Special thanks to all the contributors who have helped improve this project.
- Thanks to the open-source community for providing valuable resources and support.

## Contact

If you have any questions or suggestions, please feel free to contact us at [your-email@example.com](mailto:your-email@example.com).

Happy coding!
