   ```
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/code-correction-challenge.git
   ```

2. Navigate to the directory containing the problem you want to solve:
   ```
   cd code-correction-challenge/problem-name
   ```

3. Open the `problem-description.md` file to read the problem statement, test cases, and expected output.

4. Write your solution in the `solution.java` file. Ensure that your solution strictly consists of the corrected code only.

5. Validate your solution against the provided test cases by running the `test.sh` script:
   ```
   ./test.sh
   ```

6. If your solution passes all the test cases, you have successfully solved the problem. If not, review the test cases and make necessary adjustments to your solution.

