# Java Coding Challenge

This repository contains a collection of Java coding challenges and their solutions. Each challenge is accompanied by a detailed explanation and a solution in Java.

## Table of Contents

- [Introduction](#introduction)
- [Challenges](#challenges)
- [Contributing](#contributing)
- [License](#license)

## Introduction

Java is a widely used programming language known for its robustness and versatility. This repository provides a set of coding challenges that can help you improve your Java skills and problem-solving abilities. Each challenge includes a description, a sample input and output, and a solution in Java.

## Challenges

1. **[Challenge 1: Two Sum](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge1.md)**
   - Description: Given an array of integers `nums` and an integer `target`, return indices of the two numbers such that they add up to `target`.
   - Sample Input: `nums = [2, 7, 11, 15], target = 9`
   - Sample Output: `[0, 1]`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge1.java)

2. **[Challenge 2: Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge2.md)**
   - Description: Given a string `s`, find the length of the longest substring without repeating characters.
   - Sample Input: `s = "abcabcbb"`
   - Sample Output: `3`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge2.java)

3. **[Challenge 3: Valid Parentheses](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge3.md)**
   - Description: Given a string `s` containing just the characters `'(', ')', '{', '}', '['` and `']'`, determine if the input string is valid.
   - Sample Input: `s = "()"`
   - Sample Output: `true`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge3.java)

4. **[Challenge 4: Merge Two Sorted Lists](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge4.md)**
   - Description: Merge two sorted linked lists and return it as a new sorted list. The new list should be made by splicing together the nodes of the first two lists.
   - Sample Input: `l1 = [1, 2, 4], l2 = [1, 3, 4]`
   - Sample Output: `[1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4]`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge4.java)

5. **[Challenge 5: Longest Palindromic Substring](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge5.md)**
   - Description: Given a string `s`, return the longest palindromic substring in `s`.
   - Sample Input: `s = "babad"`
   - Sample Output: `"bab"`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge5.java)

6. **[Challenge 6: Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge6.md)**
   - Description: Given a sorted array `nums`, remove the duplicates in-place such that each element appears only once and returns the new length.
   - Sample Input: `nums = [1, 1, 2]`
   - Sample Output: `2`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge6.java)

7. **[Challenge 7: Climbing Stairs](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge7.md)**
   - Description: You are climbing a staircase. It takes `n` steps to reach the top. Each time you can either climb `1` or `2` steps. In how many distinct ways can you climb to the top?
   - Sample Input: `n = 3`
   - Sample Output: `3`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge7.java)

8. **[Challenge 8: Container With Most Water](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge8.md)**
   - Description: You are given an integer array `height` of length `n`. There are `n` vertical lines drawn such that the two endpoints of the `ith` line are `(i, 0)` and `(i, height[i])`. Find two lines that together with the x-axis form a container, such that the container contains the most water.
   - Sample Input: `height = [1, 8, 6, 2, 5, 4, 8, 3, 7]`
   - Sample Output: `49`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge8.java)

9. **[Challenge 9: Group Anagrams](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge9.md)**
   - Description: Given an array of strings `strs`, group the anagrams together. You can return the answer in any order.
   - Sample Input: `strs = ["eat", "tea", "tan", "ate", "nat", "bat"]`
   - Sample Output: `[["bat"], ["nat", "tan"], ["ate", "eat", "tea"]]`
   - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge9.java)

10. **[Challenge 10: Longest Common Prefix](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge10.md)**
    - Description: Write a function to find the longest common prefix string amongst an array of strings.
    - Sample Input: `strs = ["flower", "flow", "flight"]`
    - Sample Output: `"fl"`
    - Solution: [Java Solution](https://github.com/yourusername/java-coding-challenge/blob/main/challenge10.java)

