- [JavaScript Solutions](javascript)

## Example Solution
Here's an example of a solution in the C++ directory:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

class Solution {
public:
    std::vector<int> closestPrimes(int left, int right) {
        if (left == 1) left++;
        std::vector<bool> v(right + 1, true);
        for (int i = 2; i <= sqrt(right); i++) {
            if (v[i]) {
                for (int j = i * i; j <= right; j += i) {
                    v[j] = false;
                }
            }
        }
        int i = left;
        int j;
        int a = -1, b = -1, k = INT_MAX;
        while (i <= right) {
            if (v[i]) break;
            i++;
        }
        j = i + 1;
        while (j <= right) {
            if (v[j]) {
                if (j - i < k) {
                    k = j - i;
                    a = i, b = j;
                }
                i = j;
            }
            j++;
        }
        return {a, b};
    }
};

int main() {
    Solution solution;
    std::vector<int> result = solution.closestPrimes(10, 19);
    std::cout << "[" << result[0] << ", " << result[1] << "]" << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This example demonstrates a solution to a coding problem in C++. The `closestPrimes` function takes two integers, `left` and `right`, and returns the closest prime numbers within the given range.

## Additional Information
For more information on the coding problems and their solutions, please refer to the individual directories and README files within this repository.

Feel free to explore and contribute to this repository to help others learn and improve their coding skills.

Happy coding!
