## Example

Here is an example of a solution to a LeetCode problem:

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int reversePairs(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        int cnt = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                if (nums[i] > 2 * nums[j]) {
                    cnt++;
                }
            }
        }
        return cnt;
    }
};
```

This solution uses a brute-force approach to count the number of reverse pairs in an array. It iterates over all pairs of elements in the array and checks if the first element is greater than twice the second element. If so, it increments the count. The time complexity of this solution is O(n^2), where n is the size of the array.

