There are two approaches to solve this problem: recursive and iterative.

Recursive Approach:

In the recursive approach, we define a helper function isSymmetricHelper that takes two nodes as input and checks if they are symmetric. The base case is when both nodes are null, in which case we return true. If one of the nodes is null and the other is not, we return false. If the values of the two nodes are not equal, we return false. Otherwise, we recursively call the helper function on the left child of the first node and the right child of the second node, and on the right child of the first node and the left child of the second node. We return true if both recursive calls return true, and false otherwise.
Iterative Approach:

In the iterative approach, we use a queue to store the nodes to be checked. We start by adding the left and right children of the root node to the queue. Then, we enter a loop that continues until the queue is empty. In each iteration, we remove two nodes from the queue and check if they are symmetric. If they are not, we return false. If they are, we add their left and right children to the queue. We continue this process until the queue is empty, and return true if we reach the end of the loop.
Both approaches have a time complexity of O(n), where n is the number of nodes in the tree, and a space complexity of O(n) in the worst case, when the tree is completely unbalanced.
class Solution {
    public boolean isSymmetric(TreeNode root) {
        if (root == null) {
            return true;
        }
        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new LinkedList<>();
        queue.add(root.left);
        queue.add(root.right);
        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
            TreeNode left = queue.poll();
            TreeNode right = queue.poll();
            if (left == null && right == null) {
                continue;
            }
            if (left == null || right == null) {
                return false;
            }
            if (left.val != right.val) {
                return false;
            }
            queue.add(left.left);
            queue.add(right.right);
            queue.add(left.right);
            queue.add(right.left);
        }
        return true;
    }
}
